{"id": "finqa_dev_309", "split": "dev", "subset_source": "FinQA", "question": "Given the 5-year cumulative total return performance graph of Cadence Design Systems, Inc., what is the total return if $100,000 is invested in the S&P 500 index on January 1st, 2015, and sold at the end of 2016, considering the cumulative total return of the S&P 500 index as shown in the table?", "program_answer": 18770.00000000001, "original_answer": "1877", "company_cik": 813672, "report_year": 2018, "gold_chunk_ids": [33], "trace_id": "7734fd0d75a73be8bae69d6c60f49bc1", "trace_id_static": "36722a9ce3f3ac350b5d2d41a8300346", "session_id": "finqa_dev_309", "final_answer": "Based on the Stockholder Return Performance Graph table from Cadence Design Systems, Inc.\u2019s 2018 Form 10-K, the cumulative total return values for the S&P 500 index are:\n- **January 3, 2015 (beginning of 2015):** 110.28\n- **December 31, 2016 (end of 2016):** 129.05\n\n### Calculations:\n1. **Total Return Percentage:**\n   $$\\frac{129.05 - 110.28}{110.28} \\times 100\\% = \\frac{18.77}{110.28} \\times 100\\% \\approx 17.02\\%$$\n\n2. **Total Value of Investment at End of 2016:**\n   $$\\$100,000 \\times \\frac{129.05}{110.28} \\approx \\$117,020.31$$\n\n3. **Total Dollar Return (Gain):**\n   $$\\$117,020.31 - \\$100,000 = \\$17,020.31$$\n\nANSWER: $17,020.31", "iterations": 1, "hit_iteration_cap": false, "judge_verdicts": ["finish"], "trajectory": [{"iteration": 1, "query": "Cadence Design Systems \"cumulative total return\" \"S&P 500\" 2014 2015 2016 100", "rerank_query": "\"cumulative total return\" \"S&P 500\" 2014 2015 2016 100", "tickers": ["CDNS"], "judge_verdict": "finish", "top_k": [["CDNS_2018_813672", 33, 0.5739359259605408], ["CDNS_2006_813672", 24, 0.5196460485458374], ["CDNS_2016_813672", 31, 0.5001809597015381], ["CDNS_2015_813672", 31, 0.36512571573257446], ["CDNS_2007_813672", 25, 0.3274373710155487], ["CDNS_2012_813672", 27, 0.25322452187538147], ["CDNS_2016_813672", 84, 0.06465552002191544], [